#: ../../source/docs/calibrating-an-airspeed-sensor.rst:163
#: 5babafcd502f469d930e8b3558025e3b
msgid "Note about higher altitudes"
msgstr "关于高海拔的注意事项"

#: ../../source/docs/calibrating-an-airspeed-sensor.rst:165
#: bec43e0f83294ce793ad11fe8ab0feec
msgid ""
"At higher altitudes you expect the true airspeed and apparent airspeed to "
"start to diverge. The above calibration procedure assumes true and apparent "
"airspeed are the same. If you are flying at altitudes of 2000 meters or more"
" above sea level then you should take account of the difference, and aim for"
" your apparent airspeed to be below the average ground speed by the ratio of"
" true airspeed to apparent airspeed."
msgstr ""
"在较高海拔，真实空速和表显空速开始出现分歧是预期之事。上述校准步骤假设真实空速和表显空速相同。如果您在海拔2000米或以上飞行，则应考虑这种差异，并以表显空速低于平均地速的量等于真实空速与表显空速之比为目标。"

#: ../../source/docs/calibrating-an-airspeed-sensor.rst:172
#: 82fefe473a3c4b9896b386481f222d68
msgid ""
"At an altitude of 2000 meters above sea level the difference between "
"apparent and true airspeed is around 10%, so you would expect your average "
"airspeed to be below the average ground speed by about 10%. At 4000 meters "
"above sea level this rises to around 20%. At 5000 meters it is around 30%. "
"Beyond that please consult an aircraft navigation table."
msgstr ""
"在海拔2000米时，表显空速与真实空速之差约为10%，因此预计平均空速应比平均地速低约10%。在海拔4000米时，差值约为20%。在5000米时约为30%。更高海拔请参阅航空导航表。"
